bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899949#post899949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This invites some follow-on questions from me; what do most common folks and Dragonblooded believe about demons? How much do most folks know about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumptions: Exalted/Immaculates are the only ones who can &quot;Deal&quot; with Demons as they are the only ones &quot;Spiritually Pure&quot; enough to deal with them without being &quot;Corrupted&quot; by the Demon. Most Civilians will avoid Demons and will call for the Wyld Hunt/Immaculate Monks to deal with any Demons they find... Even &quot;Innocent&quot; ones that are generally harmless for Mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:06:59-07:00","id":899959,"title":"","content":"Trucking with and commanding demons is one of the privileges of the Exalted in general, and sorcerers in particular.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople still tend to find demons, and those who regularly associate with them, creepy.<br /> <br /> This not referring to the Anathema. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:34:35-07:00","id":899979,"title":"","content":"Although I don't recall seeing anything that stops mortals from binding them any more. So even if that's the stereotype, it's no longer entirely true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:43:04-07:00","id":899984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899979#post899979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I don't recall seeing anything that stops mortals from binding them any more. So even if that's the stereotype, it's no longer entirely true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Believe (Haven't gotten to that chapter or checked to see if it's in the Ex3 corebook) It's what the Immaculate Faith teaches. Is it possible for mortals to do it anyway? Yep. Always was (Just needed to be clever and understand the Demon your dealing with) well it was in my Games.... Not something Common but that is were Exalts can come from.... Sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:33:49-07:00","id":900060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899949#post899949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This invites some follow-on questions from me; what do most common folks and Dragonblooded believe about demons? How much do most folks know about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most common folks know they're dangerous (and extremely varied) monsters from Hell who ordinary people should have no truck with. They probably have a number of stories of different kinds of demons, a small amount of which may even be almost true.<br /> Of course, sorcerers and Dragonblood regularly deal with them... but they have the power to control them. Though in Immaculate areas, they'll argue that mortal sorcerers shouldn't deal with them, because they'll be corrupted into being infernalists.<br /> <br /> Most dynasts will likely have enough occult learning to vaguely have an idea of some of the more commonly seen demons, (I imagine the House of Bells occasionally does classes about how to fight Blood Apes, for example), and know generalities (like how dematerialising works), but generally speaking only Heptagram graduates will have a detailed understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:55:27-07:00","id":900093,"title":"","content":"Regarding the OP, I would note that, as DBs have a roughly 300 year lifespan and look like they're in their 20s to 40s for most of it, I'd imagine that dating someone young enough to be your great grandson/daughter is pretty common, but, yes, having sex with your kids is not allowed. I could see House Cynis not making a big deal about it, but they're the only ones I could really see ignoring it.<br /> <br /> Also, Cynis Anbor from AB:Wood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:02:22-07:00","id":900102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899906#post899906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be about as big a scandal in the Realm as everywhere else in the world throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies you would reveal the information instead of blackmail.... not a very fitting course of action for an up and coming Senator...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:05:06-07:00","id":900107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900093#post900093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the OP, I would note that, as DBs have a roughly 300 year lifespan and look like they're in their 20s to 40s for most of it, I'd imagine that dating someone young enough to be your great grandson/daughter is pretty common, but, yes, having sex with your kids is not allowed. I could see House Cynis not making a big deal about it, but they're the only ones I could really see ignoring it.<br /> <br /> Also, Cynis Anbor from AB:Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine like in real life, the older you get, the less age matters. The Age gap between 16 and 26 is creepy and between 45 and 55 isn't too bad. 90 and 100 would merit a newspaper article about how sweet it is that someone found love at that age. So for Dragonblooded, 60 and 120 maybe turn a few heads. 150 and 220 would barely be note worthy.<br /> <br /> I head canon that after you age out of a mortal lifetime, age doesn't matter. It is the events you live though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:54:25-07:00","id":900144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900093#post900093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see House Cynis not making a big deal about it, but they're the only ones I could really see ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'll be interested in way that House Cynis might develop in this Edition.<br /> <br /> Like the possibility that the debauched parties might be more about creating a ready venue for collecting secrets.<br /> <br /> Or that their reputation for vulgarity is something that comes from displaying a lot of barbarian foreign customs picked up from their business interests in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> It seems likely to me that most Dynasts will treat sexual abuse of their children as a shameful, disturbing thing that they would rather cover up or quietly enable than go through the emotional tumults of exposing and dealing with.<br /> <br /> Especially if any abusers are in positions of significant authority or prestige.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:11:44-07:00","id":900153,"title":"","content":"So the line about DBs being casual about sexually abusing their own kids never made it to print? Didn't think so. Thank you all for the information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:11:45-07:00","id":900154,"title":"","content":"I would like to note that a number of cultures, among them ancient Egyptian and...certain Polynesian? considered brother-sister incest to be okay. Heck, the pharaohs were obliged to do it. Parent-child incest is pretty much a universal taboo, though. Of course, that doesn't account for the possible age difference between children who could be a century apart, but that stops being cultural norms and starts going into the power dynamics of abuse, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:15:24-07:00","id":900160,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would definitely expect Creation'ers (Creationists? Creatures? Creationteers?) to often have dissimilar ideas about what constitutes verboten levels of incest, and that parent-child relations be too extreme for most people whose speech bubbles don't have black backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:38:45-07:00","id":900451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899946#post899946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that pretty much the entire purpose of Neomah?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> no you are thinking of that bug-body/human face'd demon/evil spirit from Avatar: The last airbender","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:45:08-07:00","id":900460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900451#post900451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> no you are thinking of that bug-body/human face'd demon/evil spirit from Avatar: The last airbender</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Jet was referring taking demons to bed, not demons that steal faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:59:18-07:00","id":900475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900460#post900460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Jet was referring taking demons to bed, not demons that steal faces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love has no boundaries tho","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:03:09-07:00","id":900478,"title":"","content":"Also, face-stealing demons already exist - they're called Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:24:34-07:00","id":900498,"title":"","content":"Really, thinking more about the jab towards Hollywood...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, I think this is getting frank to a point where it needs to be put behind a layer of preparation, so:<br /> <br /> \u200bTrigger warning for somewhat frank discussion of the circumstances of rape apologia, and how that might pertain to frequency of rape amongst the Exalted:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> \u200bI think the extent to which the Exalted being perceived as generally visionaries, geniuses and artists as an accurate rendition of this has significance to considering this topic.<br /> <br /> If the instances in which somebody who has created some widely beloved or highly regarded artistic work, or other achievement, is then accused with strong credibility or outright proven to have engaged in sexual abuse or assault... well, if the responses to that are not always mixed, then they're at least frequent enough (particularly with particularly prestigious figures) to depict an unhappy and significant trend.<br /> <br /> I do not think it is much of a stretch to assume that many Dynasts would prefer not to know if the peer who writes their favourite poetry (and it really is beautiful poetry) ever sexually assaulted a child, prefer not to have to think about whether or not that makes it all right to still read the poems, or any new ones that are published.<br /> <br /> Or if not about artistic merit, but practical achievements; if a highly decorated and skilled general, who is a true and stalwart servant of the Realm and defender of precious satrapies... I think many would not want to even deal with the question of replacing them and removing their skills from a key place.<br /> <br /> It's not a case of saying &quot;all Dynasts/Exalted are rapists as even they would acknowledge the term&quot; (compared to ones who would have sex with slaves), but rather than if all Exalted have some of those qualities that people might commend them for, then it means that any rapists amongst them will have those qualities that tend to interfere with how people respond to rapists.<br /> <br /> Particularly considering that the Realm and Dynasty are not likely to have our perspective on things like human rights or consent; that's not a case of them being okay with it, more that they might not have a very sophisticated way of articulating and describing it (although there will also be forms of rape that they refer to as rape that they will be basically all right with, such as its use in warfare and towards subdued enemies and subjects, because they have different attitudes to the application of violence as well).<br /> <br /> Likewise, this is not me trying to make an argument that rape and abuse are complicated things or the idea of presenting characters who would be rapists but also &quot;good people&quot; (or useful people).<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to illustrate factors, that I think are important for how we consider the real world, that would interfere with how people in the setting might respond to sexual predators, and how such distractions are liable to be typically present with the Exalted.<br /> <br /> It all makes me feel very uncomfortable, as well as worried that I'm appropriating real life pains for the sake of abstract intellectual arguments, but... I think they're important factors to circulate in consideration.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-26-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:12:50-07:00","id":900520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900451#post900451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> no you are thinking of that bug-body/human face'd demon/evil spirit from Avatar: The last airbender</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah what Kyman said. Sex demons, not face stealing demons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:26:28-07:00","id":900525,"title":"","content":"As regards the original subject...<br /> <br /> \u200bTrigger warning for discussion of vulnerability of children to sexual assault and resulting traumas:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Dynasts having sex with their own children, and often with the children of others, is going to be a subject of outrage and disgust if ever openly discussed in the Scarlet Dynasty, but the fact will remain that children are extremely vulnerable in a context of significant violence and exploitation; measures that Dynast parents might go to protect their children don't mitigate this, they illustrate it.<br /> <br /> The prior post talked about people who might engage in sexual violence towards whomever and get away with it because of their prestige or positions, and I would generally assume that such people have a natural impulse.<br /> <br /> But I think the society of the Dynasty would foster a lot of resentment and bitterness in its members who never Exalted, and such might create a tendency from some to seek violent expressions of power over others who are not only highly vulnerable, but might draw resentment from perceptions of having opportunities lost to the abusers.<br /> <br /> Especially when it's noted that unExalted adults are given positions of responsibility over those children.<br /> <br /> Maybe that only takes place prior to Exaltation, maybe it continues into a period when their power is still unrefined, on occasion it could conceivably last the mortal's lifetime. It will differ between cases, as these things do. I would say it's also more complicated than just &quot;once they're Exalted, they use that power to take revenge&quot;; I mean, it would happen sometimes, maybe disproportionately often, just as a matter of how different people respond to assault and abuse in different ways and the Exalted might be more powerful than is typical of people who have been victimized and would have an impulse for revenge, but I would think there are cases where it doesn't quite happen that way. Sometimes, the newly Exalted might have confused, distorted feelings about what happened, not even really being able to fully recognise it for what it. Sometimes they'll view the idea of having been abused in such a way by a mortal with shame and not want to take any chance of revealing it. Sometimes the unExalted will be a person of high reputation by the standards of a mortal in the Dynasty, where simply destroying them without explanation cannot be countenanced and others will not hear a word against them. Sometimes, no amount of genuine desire to take violent revenge from a reversed power position will help with being conditioned to flinch away every time you look at somebody.<br /> <br /> I want to emphasize, I'm not saying that the experience of Dynastic childhood would be or should be wall-to-wall abuse, just that in cases where it could happen (and, considering how small the Dynasty is, even if such cases are few, they can stand out), there could be more to it than many people would recognise, and the Dynasty contains details that look to me as though they would enable it.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:26:46-07:00","id":900567,"title":"","content":"I generally play up the sexually liberal culture of the Realm in my games...and mother/son incest was never even on my radar. It's going to stay off it. Ick.<br /> <br /> I do agree this is the kind of boundary Cynis would transgress, though in private.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:48:26-07:00","id":900591,"title":"","content":"There's Ragara Heral, who's in a romantic relationship with his (male) cousin. That's kind of of squick. I guess if it worked for FDR...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1453-henry","name":"Henry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:51:58-07:00","id":900592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Henry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900591#post900591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's Ragara Heral, who's in a romantic relationship with his (male) cousin. That's kind of of squick. I guess if it worked for FDR...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know Ragra Heral in particular, but given that almost every Dynast is cousin to another Dynast, I'm not sure that's going to be an issue for them (assuming it's not like first cousin or something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T20:10:44-07:00","id":900616,"title":"","content":"Doing it with your cousins is part of the theme of aristocracy that Dragonblood (or at least Dynasts) channel, just like blood purity, wealth, everyone being a soldier even if they're a bureaucrat, and being a dick. Queen Victoria married her first cousin. Queen Elizabeth is married to her third cousin/second cousin once-removed (and when you can trace your relationship through two seperate ways, you know it's too close).<br /> Hey, in some parts of the world, marrying your (first) cousin is still pretty common.<br /> <br /> Whereas in no culture I can think of did anyone marry their mum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-26-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T23:00:52-07:00","id":900716,"title":"","content":"What about all the crippling genetic defects? Like, is there a Dynastic equivalent to Carlos II of Spain?<br /> <br /> Is it Fokuf? Because that would actually explain a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T23:19:13-07:00","id":900721,"title":"","content":"Could well be.<br /> Or maybe the exaltation burns out this kind of thing from their bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T23:53:46-07:00","id":900739,"title":"","content":"This is one of the many places where I assume &quot;human nature&quot; in Creation is the same as it is in real life, so abuses that happen in the real world happen in Creation at roughly the same frequency given similar social contexts, but I'm really not pushing for the books to spotlight it because man we have better things to devote words to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T00:45:56-07:00","id":900758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900739#post900739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the many places where I assume &quot;human nature&quot; in Creation is the same as it is in real life, so abuses that happen in the real world happen in Creation at roughly the same frequency given similar social contexts, but I'm really not pushing for the books to spotlight it because man we have better things to devote words to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily you guys already recommended <i>The Black Company</i> (see: the bits in which members of the titular Company let some steam off with murder, rape and arson, and Croaker intentionally turns an editorial blind eye to it all because they're his brothers in arms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-27-2016, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T00:58:30-07:00","id":900764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900716#post900716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about all the crippling genetic defects? Like, is there a Dynastic equivalent to Carlos II of Spain?<br /> <br /> Is it Fokuf? Because that would actually explain a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we dont know for sure if genetics works the same in Creation. DNA may not be a thing, instead heredity may be cartied by motes of Essence energy or something. So inbreeding may not be a thing. Considering the extent the Dynasty is all related to a still living woman, though, I think it isnt or maybe less imoactful.<br /> <br /> But, that may not be nough forvthem to escape the Upper Class Twit trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:43:25-07:00","id":900781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900616#post900616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing it with your cousins is part of the theme of aristocracy that Dragonblood (or at least Dynasts) channel, just like blood purity, wealth, everyone being a soldier even if they're a bureaucrat, and being a dick. Queen Victoria married her first cousin. Queen Elizabeth is married to her third cousin/second cousin once-removed (and when you can trace your relationship through two seperate ways, you know it's too close).<br /> Hey, in some parts of the world, marrying your (first) cousin is still pretty common.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anglo-Irish gentry side of my ancestry went in for it a fair bit, apparently. Possibly a bit too much; some of them were getting <i>pretty</i> eccentric by the beginning of the 20th century. But I'm always faintly confused by the strength of the reaction cousin-marriage gets in some quarters: it's not like they're marrying the sister of their deceased wife or something [1]...<br /> <br /> [1] <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deceased_Wife&#39;s_Sister&#39;s_Marriage_Act_1907\" target=\"_blank\">19th century Anglicanism joke. </a>It's worth noting that similar concerns applied in Imperial China, eg. in 'The Dream of the Red Chamber' there's a strong implication that one character suicides because her relationship with one of her in-laws is not only adulterous, but would be considered incestious due to the link by marriage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:58:54-07:00","id":900785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900716#post900716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about all the crippling genetic defects? Like, is there a Dynastic equivalent to Carlos II of Spain?<br /> <br /> Is it Fokuf? Because that would actually explain a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somewhere back in 1st ed it mentioned that the exaltation solved the inbreeding problem with those whole exalted, can't remember where though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T02:07:31-07:00","id":900787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Henry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900591#post900591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's Ragara Heral, who's in a romantic relationship with his (male) cousin. That's kind of of squick. I guess if it worked for FDR...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like they're going to have any kids. What's the problem, really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T03:30:34-07:00","id":900810,"title":"","content":"You know, while no culture approves of Parent/offspring relations, some (most notably Ancient Egypt) did allow sibling marriage. Think there is anything like that in Creation?<br /> <br /> Probably not the Dynasty though. They seem to view marriage as a mechanism of political alliances, so that would be counter productive to such a purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 07-30-2017, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:18:42-07:00","id":900839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899916#post899916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I have to write up a demon that steals faces.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, a Lunar?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:25:10-07:00","id":900844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900839#post900839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, a Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Already said that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:25:56-07:00","id":900845,"title":"","content":"Maybe literally steals faces. As in you have no face after the demon is done with you. Just a blank expanse of skin over skull. You have to cut a hole for your mouth if you wish to eat*.<br /> <br /> Or maybe have someone go on a quest to retrieve your face from the demon. <br /> <br /> *Okay... Maybe too horrorish for Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:41:21-07:00","id":900853,"title":"","content":"So basically a lame episode of doctor who?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:42:37-07:00","id":900854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900853#post900853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically a lame episode of doctor who?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparently my RPG stories are a lot more campy than your RPG stories. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-27-2016, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:45:06-07:00","id":900855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900764#post900764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we dont know for sure if genetics works the same in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works similarly <i>enough</i>. Inheritable traits are passed down through generations - sometimes traits are dominant, sometimes they're recessive, and both inbreeding and congenital birth defects exist in the setting. The biggest differences observable are that <i>sometimes</i> these traits are magical, and that sometimes, <i>sometimes</i>, you get <b>very</b> unusual, unexpected, often singular results\u2026 which even then might just be the gods, demons, the Wyld, et cetera.. dicking around with ya.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900764#post900764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DNA may not be a thing, instead heredity may be cartied by motes of Essence energy or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if DNA specifically isn't a thing, it doesn't mean anything is the slightest bit different in terms of results. Also, cells are a thing, so DNA also being a thing doesn't sound all that far-fetched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900764#post900764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So inbreeding may not be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Inbreeding</i>, see <i>Lintha</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900764#post900764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the extent the Dynasty is all related to a still living woman, though, I think it isnt or maybe less imoactful.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's a vagina, not the Cave of Wonders.&quot; <br /> <br /> Also, chances of getting bad genes from inbreeding really start to plummet once you hit &quot;Second cousin once removed&quot; territory. The Dynasty is big enough (and contains enough mortals besides) that the genes of their <i>one</i> common ancestor as many as a dozen generations back is <i>generally</i> a remote threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-27-2016, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:49:24-07:00","id":900858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900855#post900855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, chances of getting bad genes from inbreeding really start to plummet once you hit &quot;Second cousin once removed&quot; territory. The Dynasty is big enough (and contains enough mortals besides) that the genes of their <i>one</i> common ancestor as many as a dozen generations back is <i>generally</i> a remote threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did Me and 23 a few months back. I only share like 5% of my DNA with my second cousin. I don't think inbreeding is a big deal for the Realm, though I'm sure that won't stop Lookshy from making bad jokes about it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:03:43-07:00","id":900865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900787#post900787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like they're going to have any kids. What's the problem, really?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoever said sexual taboos were rational? Anti-incest is buried deep enough in human psychology that people will react as badly to incest that could create kids as to that which can't.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as Iozz-Sothoth said, it was pretty common in the past to marry your first cousin.<br /> <br /> Actually, in some parts of the Indian subcontinent it's still common. There are ethnic Indians in Britain who are married to their first cousins. Perfectly legal. Not something doctor's would advise, but it doesn't cause them massive problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:13:33-07:00","id":900872,"title":"","content":"Really, in the first generation the effects are basically negligible. You need them to build up over a really long time to produce serious problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:24:44-07:00","id":900879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900739#post900739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the many places where I assume &quot;human nature&quot; in Creation is the same as it is in real life, so abuses that happen in the real world happen in Creation at roughly the same frequency given similar social contexts, but I'm really not pushing for the books to spotlight it because man we have better things to devote words to.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this were 90's WW, though there would be not-so-oblique references all up in this bitch. Gotta stay edgy, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:36:11-07:00","id":900891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900844#post900844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already said that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> What, a Sidereal, Infernal or Abyssal?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:54:34-07:00","id":900963,"title":"","content":"I believe I have seen some references to it in 2ed, but it was more hinted at than spelled out. Can't find it at the moment, so it can be &quot;Internet knowledge&quot; instead of from the books.<br /> <br /> However, 2ed has that a Dynast child is removed from the mother and more or less are raised by wet-nurses, and then raised by another family, which would mean no eventual Westermarck effect to kick in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westermarck_effect\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westermarck_effect</a><br /> <br /> The Realm also states that Dragon-bloods are more morally pure, so a lot of things forbidden for mortals are considered legal, even if not always acceptable, for Dynasts. So they have the perfect tool to rationalize it for themselves.<br /> <br /> So I would say, at least when it comes to 2ed, it is just a matter of how a specific gaming group want to set the dials for how common and how much in focus it should be.<br /> <br /> My own take on the setting, if it would become public it would result in a lot of gossip, and the risk of having some raving about how it is against the Immaculate texts, maybe but not necessary a loss of position at &quot;work&quot;. This added on top of being caught with an adulterous affair, as it can mean a political scandal between Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:55:29-07:00","id":900965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900144#post900144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'll be interested in way that House Cynis might develop in this Edition.<br /> <br /> Like the possibility that the debauched parties might be more about creating a ready venue for collecting secrets.<br /> <br /> Or that their reputation for vulgarity is something that comes from displaying a lot of barbarian foreign customs picked up from their business interests in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> It seems likely to me that most Dynasts will treat sexual abuse of their children as a shameful, disturbing thing that they would rather cover up or quietly enable than go through the emotional tumults of exposing and dealing with.<br /> <br /> Especially if any abusers are in positions of significant authority or prestige.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted 1E, Core Book, page 40: &quot;While the behavior of some nobles and senators at Cynis gatherings might make excellent fodder for blackmail, the Cynises guarantee that whatever occurs at one of their soirees stays there. This discretion puts them in an implied position of power over their guests and seems like a boon, even though the Cynises haven't actually done anything.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exalted 1E, DB book, page 89: &quot;House Cynis has learned enough about the Dynasts and patricians who attend its discreet orgies by now to know which ones have &quot;unnatural&quot; tastes. The Cynises now quietly offer certain services to their favorite politicians and allies that would make the patrons very unpopular if the general public found out. Thanks to their location in rutal Pangu, they have plenty of open land on which to bury slaves' bodies.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first thing isn't a development, that's always been there. I like the idea of them picking up foreign customs though there's quite a few Houses that would be susceptible to that (Ledaal and Peleps both come to mind).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:20:26-07:00","id":900990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=900855#post900855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works similarly <i>enough</i>. Inheritable traits are passed down through generations - sometimes traits are dominant, sometimes they're recessive...</div> </div> </div> </div>...and sometimes more complex than that. Interesting to note, but a lot of what we thought were once rather simple cases of drawing up Punnet squares to predict combinations aren't so simple, like anything involving hair, eye, or skin pigmentation, so another quote of Holden's talking about some happenstances that he regarded as genetically impossible (getting a hero's unusual hair color when their other parent's traits would seem to overwhelm it) is merely improbable or slightly less usual.<br /> <br /> Except for the anime hair colors. It's open season on how those interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:34:43-07:00","id":901005,"title":"","content":"yes while Cynis is incredibly depraved, I don't think they cause any incest. Note that the quote indicates slaves and relations are used to satisfy those depravities.<br /> <br /> Back to the incest problem. With the lengthen spans and the incentive to breed, would they get as bad as King Charles the 8th of Spain? <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Charles_II_of_Spain#/media/File:Carlos_segundo80.png\" target=\"_blank\">This family tree</a> from wikimedia shows how interlinked his family was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:49:53-07:00","id":901026,"title":"","content":"Probably not.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the dynasty has 10,000 Dragon-Blood, plus mortal members. The genetic pool is actually far bigger than what medieval monarchs were looking for. There's a reason that Henry VIII was forced by his dad to marry Catherine of Aragon, rather than just marry another Spanish princess: there wasn't one.<br /> There was actually a point in the middle ages when a bunch of western monarchs married Byzantine Princesses, because there just wasn't any princesses in western Europe they were legally allowed to marry (due to Catholic rules about consanguanity).<br /> <br /> Secondly, the dynasts are (probably) almost all descended from the Scarlet Empress by now, but they're not necessarily descended from a)her through many different lines, and b)other people who cross-over in the genetic record.<br /> When the great-grandson of Tepet and the great-grandaughter of Mnemon marry, chances are reasonable that the Scarlet Empress is the only ancestor they share. It's possible they might share one or two others, but it's not very certain.<br /> It's actually possible there are very old Dynasts who aren't descended from the Scarlet Empress. I mean, senior members of House Tepet might well be descended from Tepet's sister, brother, or cousin, a family of Dragonblood who all got promoted to Dynast when their relative married the Empress and got given his own House. I'd think by now almost all dynasts would be descended from the Scarlet Empress, but likely just the once.<br /> Related to this, is the fact that there are not many inter-house marriages. Medieval aristocrats would often marry their cousin or second-cousin to keep property in the noble house, but it seems the Dynasty normally marries across Houses. This is probably partly because the male stays in his own House, so the Houses aren't losing people by marrying them off, just that they won't produce children for the house.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, the Dynasty regularly gets infusions of peasant blood. Officially, the peasant who just exalted is a long-lost son of someone's dead brother, but really that's a legal fiction. He might marry another Dynastic Dragonblood if he's particularly heroic or lucky, but more likely he'll just marry a mortal Dynast. But that still infuses the Dynasty with outside blood.<br /> <br /> Lastly, medieval aristocrats often married closely due to property rights. Since woman couldn't inherit in German Salic law, it was pretty common for a man to try to marry his daughter to his nephew (who was going to inherit the property), as I understand it. There were more general attempts to consolidate property by close marriages, and marriages to people far from the family could well mean the family would &quot;lose&quot; property.<br /> But with dynastic inheritance, this seems to be less of an issue.<br /> So there's not the incentive to marry closely, rather there's the incentive to marry into other Houses to secure diplomacy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:52:00-07:00","id":901030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901005#post901005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the incest problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between all this incest discussion and the amputation-fetish thread, I'm beginning to think we as a forum have issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901005#post901005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the lengthen spans and the incentive to breed, would they get as bad as King Charles the 8th of Spain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer: No. Longer answer: No; the sheer number of people in the Scarlet Dynasty is seriously going to inhibit genetic bottle-necking like that. Moreover, the &quot;incentive to breed&quot; is not an incentive to <i>in</i>breed (both because there's dozens to hundreds of other candidates with just as good pedigrees that <i>aren't</i> a sibling or first cousin, <i>and</i> because a great portion marriage system in the Realm is about cementing bonds with other Houses, and there's little benefit in cementing yourself to yourself).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd because I stopped to check your link. Wizard also said it better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-27-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:53:43-07:00","id":901033,"title":"","content":"I don't even know what this thread is about anymore. A forumite asked a question and it got answered. How did we get 2 more pages after that? Sometimes I think we (as a forum) are starved for debate in our lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:59:13-07:00","id":901036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901005#post901005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes while Cynis is incredibly depraved, I don't think they cause any incest. Note that the quote indicates slaves and relations are used to satisfy those depravities.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happens at a Cynis party stays at a Cynis party.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back to the incest problem. With the lengthen spans and the incentive to breed, would they get as bad as King Charles the 8th of Spain? <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Charles_II_of_Spain#/media/File:Carlos_segundo80.png\" target=\"_blank\">This family tree</a> from wikimedia shows how interlinked his family was. </div> </div> </div>I would say it depend a bit on how many political marriages that are between the Great Houses, and how many that are between different families within a Great House. The former would probably make it less so, while the later definitely puts it in the Habsburgian ball-park.<br /> <br /> Still, there is probably at least one Satrapsy with a Ptolemyan family trees, so the Dynasts can still point their fingers and roll their eyes at someone else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:15:35-07:00","id":901057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901026#post901026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to this, is the fact that there are not many inter-house marriages. Medieval aristocrats would often marry their cousin or second-cousin to keep property in the noble house, but it seems the Dynasty normally marries across Houses. This is probably partly because the male stays in his own House, so the Houses aren't losing people by marrying them off, just that they won't produce children for the house.</div> </div> </div> </div>This had me confused -- I think you mean there are few int<i>ra</i>-House marriages and lots of int<i>er</i>-House marriages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:24:52-07:00","id":901064,"title":"","content":"Not sure the norm would be to marry between the Great Houses, as that would in my opinion remove to much of the tension between them. Female and male Dynasts are to equal. It had been another thing if the woman was married off, and then counts as a member of the new family.<br /> <br /> So I would say the norm is more likely to be marriages between families within a Great House. But as they are still political, marriages will not be between very close relatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:58:50-07:00","id":901099,"title":"","content":"I am pretty sure a dynast does not take his or her spouse's name. Kids take their mother's family name, but their father keeps whatever his family name always was. In this way, neither are really 'married off' to another Great House.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I am radically remembering wrong.<br /> <br /> Edit: an example of this is Ledaal Kes. His wife is Ragara Szaya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","user":"GSD","date":". 05-27-2016, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:20:45-07:00","id":901188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901064#post901064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure the norm would be to marry between the Great Houses, as that would in my opinion remove to much of the tension between them. Female and male Dynasts are to equal. It had been another thing if the woman was married off, and then counts as a member of the new family.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Empress wants *just* enough tension between Houses, not too much, and cross-House alliances supported by marriage (and cross-House Sworn Brotherhoods, which are the default) are a way of making sure that there are enough connections between Houses to keep tensions from spiralling out of control. (Houses do tend have particular Houses that they tend to marry into as well, reflecting common alliances.) From a gaming and realism perspective, this provides a lot of the Byzantine social complexity that's needed in order to prevent Dynastic politics from being too clear-cut, as it means that characters have personal ties of loyalty and honour beyond those of their Houses, which also reflects how these things operate in RL. <br /> <br /> From a historical perspective, for instance, most of the Welsh Royal Houses intermarried with each other, with the Irish, and with the Normans, and it really didn't stop them from having <i>extremely </i>tense relationships with each other or going to war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:24:08-07:00","id":901193,"title":"","content":"Some parts from 2ed, MoEP: Dragon-Blooded on this topic<br /> <br /> p.22<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this time of uncertainty in particular, the Great Houses<br /> are intermarrying at an astonishing rate in hopes of making one<br /> last round of alliances before the storm that\u2019s brewing breaks and<br /> changes the Realm forever. </div> </div> </div>Which I read as marriage between the houses was far from the norm before that.<br /> <br /> p.32<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is said that the best lovers<br /> on the Blessed Isle descend from Cynis Falen, and Falen herself is<br /> quite proud of that reputation because she has trained most of her<br /> descendents in the arts of love at one point or another. </div> </div> </div>This could be theoretical pointers.<br /> <br /> p.32<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One House, Sesus, regularly marries into Cynis, but even<br /> that has its political disadvantages at times. </div> </div> </div>And even less the norm for house Cynis.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it isn't like 2ed never contradicted itself. So even if people want to go by setting as written, there are probably some good texts saying something completely different. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:39:05-07:00","id":901207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901188#post901188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a historical perspective, for instance, most of the Welsh Royal Houses intermarried with each other, with the Irish, and with the Normans, and it really didn't stop them from having <i>extremely </i>tense relationships with each other or going to war.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how many of those where examples of men changing House, and then were considered loyal to their new House?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that never happen, and that it never happens in Exalted. Just that if 40% of the Exalts in your own house comes from another House, then there probably wouldn't be that much of a house uniqueness, and there probably just would be a House Scarlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:27:43-07:00","id":901399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901207#post901207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how many of those where examples of men changing House, and then were considered loyal to their new House?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would be the women changing House, and one assumes (modulo Welsh divorce law, which was liberal for the time) that they'd be at least nominally loyal to their husbands, as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gwenllian_ferch_Gruffydd\" target=\"_blank\">Gwenllian ferch Gruffydd of House Aberffraw</a> was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901207#post901207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that never happen, and that it never happens in Exalted. Just that if 40% of the Exalts in your own house comes from another House, then there probably wouldn't be that much of a house uniqueness, and there probably just would be a House Scarlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Male Exalts don't 'leave' their Houses as such [1] -- they're always part of their birth House. But House membership is matrilineal, so unless it's a male Dynastic DB married to a mortal female Dynast, children will be members of the mother's House, not their father's.<br /> <br /> [1] 1E, which is probably a more reliable source than 2E, observes that newly weds can live in either House's holdings or head off to form a new household of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:16:06-07:00","id":901444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901033#post901033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I think we are starved for debate in our lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHehehehehe<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:23:49-07:00","id":901451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901026#post901026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medieval aristocrats would often marry their cousin or second-cousin to keep property in the noble house, but it seems the Dynasty normally marries across Houses. This is probably partly because the male stays in his own House, so the Houses aren't losing people by marrying them off, just that they won't produce children for the house.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt probably helps that Dynasts don't really get much from inheritance, and generally have to make their money be actually working for a living.<br /> <br /> I imagine there are more benefits to marrying into another House in order to foster relationships that can share resources; marry your son to a Ragara if you want his assets to have better investment opportunities. Likewise, the benefits you can draw from offering access to your own materials to another House's children (who will also have an intimate connection to yourselves that can be drawn upon in future).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:26:45-07:00","id":901454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901451#post901451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt probably helps that Dynasts don't really get much from inheritance, and generally have to make their money be actually working for a living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this because of their longevity, or a societal design by the Empress aiming to make them more expansionistic?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:33:54-07:00","id":901462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901454#post901454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this because of their longevity, or a societal design by the Empress aiming to make them more expansionistic?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI would say probably both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T19:22:18-07:00","id":901651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901033#post901033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know what this thread is about anymore. A forumite asked a question and it got answered. How did we get 2 more pages after that? Sometimes I think we (as a forum) are starved for debate in our lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Living in China, I actually am starved for debate in my life. I freely admit that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This had me confused -- I think you mean there are few int<i>ra</i>-House marriages and lots of int<i>er</i>-House marriages.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are quite right, I apologise. What a poor English teacher I am.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSD</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am pretty sure a dynast does not take his or her spouse's name. Kids take their mother's family name, but their father keeps whatever his family name always was. In this way, neither are really 'married off' to another Great House.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I am radically remembering wrong.<br /> <br /> Edit: an example of this is Ledaal Kes. His wife is Ragara Szaya.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, that is how it works. So less reason to make sure people are married within the same family. Actually, most of the NPC write-ups for Dynasts mention their parents as being from two different houses, though some are only from one. And Cynis Negezzer's father is a time-traveller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I read as marriage between the houses was far from the norm before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean it wasn't fairly common before, just that maybe it's more common.<br /> Or it could just mean they're marrying off all their singletons quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this because of their longevity, or a societal design by the Empress aiming to make them more expansionistic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Isator, probably both. Plus the fact that Dragon-blood are the sort who go out and do things, not just sit on their arses collecting rent money, reinforcing this kind of culture.<br /> <br /> Also, what with the way stipends (and the 2nd ed Arsenal background) work, I think probably an awful lot of property belongs to the <i>House</i>, not individuals. I note that the Houses, in 2e at least, had quite discrete areas of the Isle, not the patchwork randomness you got with medieval dynasties. House Nellens mostly live together in a giant sprawling manor (at least in 2e... I think that's kind of weird, honestly, but anyway).<br /> So these indicate to me that a lot of Dynasts, while they do own stuff themselves, don't own as much as you might think, as the buildings they live in, the businesses they run, etc, belong to the House. So, if a senior male banker in House Ragara dies, the money he's made is split between his Pelleps kids, but he was mostly making money for his House, which stays in-House.<br /> Essentially, Houses are corporations, and can own things* by themselves.<br /> <br /> *Pre-modern laws are generally a mess of tradition, de-facto effects, and unwritten rules. It's possible that some Houses work like this and some don't. I could especially see the houses run by their founders as actually consisting of property belonging to their founder. So, Mnemon herself actually owns everything in House Mnemon, Ragara owns everything in Ragara, etc. Meaning that upon their deaths, the economics of inheritance will be rather messy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T20:09:00-07:00","id":901677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901651#post901651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Cynis Negezzer's father is a time-traveller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Writers-goofed-up-his-timeline time-traveller, or actual-in-setting time-traveller?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T20:42:58-07:00","id":901695,"title":"","content":"I assume the first. But I like to imagine it's the second.<br /> <br /> Or maybe he's a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T20:53:29-07:00","id":901701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded#post899895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all.<br /> <br /> Question: I am not sure if I'm going insane, and I am sorry for the squick, but I distinctly recall a reference something like &quot;the Realm is a place where a mother may take her son to bed with her&quot; regarding the dragon blooded. I think this might have been the VERY early, pre-publishing, lore posts from back before nWoD. Did this actually make it into the books, and if so, does anyone know if the 3e Dragon Blooded are intended to be at the same level of squickiness or less?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't remember the exact source, but it's the type of thing that gets spread in rumors about one's political enemies, or among other people's about the Dynasty, but it's not an actual accepted norm. Pretty much like Ancient Rome in that regard. We have the IDEA of these horrible depraved orgies, but the context of their recording means that even if they did happen they were a violation of social taboos, not an actual accepted norm.<br /> <br /> Anything closer than first-cousins is going to be taboo in the Realm. Not that it doesn't ever happen - but it will be viewed scandalously.<br /> <br /> That said, I think marriage between cousins of different households in the same Great House are relatively common.<br /> <br /> <br /> CAVEAT: That someone with enough power can freely sexually abuse those they wield power over and get away with it, is unfortunately found all through human society and history, and the Realm isn't going to be any different in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-28-2016, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T21:45:25-07:00","id":901728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That someone with enough power can freely sexually abuse those they wield power over and get away with it, is unfortunately found all through human society and history, and the Realm isn't going to be any different in that regard. </div> </div> </div>I would think though, that due to the way dynastic kids are raised by nannies, relatives, etc, while I wouldn't say it would never happen, dynastic paedophiles are more likely to abuse peasant or slave kids than their own, as they have much more power over them.<br /> Not saying that's any better, just that it's not incest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T00:41:24-07:00","id":901847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901399#post901399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it would be the women changing House, and one assumes (modulo Welsh divorce law, which was liberal for the time) that they'd be at least nominally loyal to their husbands, as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gwenllian_ferch_Gruffydd\" target=\"_blank\">Gwenllian ferch Gruffydd of House Aberffraw</a> was</div> </div> </div> </div>While women during medieval times probably had more power than most think, it was still a far stretch from a marriage between equals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Male Exalts don't 'leave' their Houses as such [1] -- they're always part of their birth House. But House membership is matrilineal, so unless it's a male Dynastic DB married to a mortal female Dynast, children will be members of the mother's House, not their father's.<br /> <br /> [1] 1E, which is probably a more reliable source than 2E, observes that newly weds can live in either House's holdings or head off to form a new household of their own. </div> </div> </div>Ah, interesting. I however don't see 1ed as more reliable than 2ed, but that they have a different idea when writing. I assume Ex3 will come up with a third variant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As with most other thing, I personally prefer the 2ed version over the 1ed version, and mainly read 1ed and Ex3 to mine for ideas.I personally find it much more interesting if both males and females can be married into another family line within a Greater House, or change Greater House, which would lead to quite some negotiations on whom will be married away. That is how I interpret 2ed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901651#post901651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't mean it wasn't fairly common before, just that maybe it's more common.<br /> Or it could just mean they're marrying off all their singletons quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> Which also means it is an ambiguous text, making it more diable while still be setting as written. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The drawback is that everyone in a new group might have very different expectations, making it more important to talk about them even if going by setting as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T03:06:50-07:00","id":901914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901728#post901728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think though, that due to the way dynastic kids are raised by nannies, relatives, etc, while I wouldn't say it would never happen, dynastic paedophiles are more likely to abuse peasant or slave kids than their own, as they have much more power over them.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI have two thoughts on this.<br /> <br /> One is that I thiiiink not all people who sexually abuse their own children are paedophiles, at least in a general sense.<br /> <br /> The other... well, before I can make a point precisely, I would need to ask if you're suggesting that the Dynasts won't do it because they barely ever see their children, or because the nannies et al. would be undesired witnesses, even implicit or explicit protectors?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T04:43:28-07:00","id":901954,"title":"","content":"Mostly the first. Perhaps with a bit of the second: I mean, nannies would obviously not criticise a Dragonblood, but if asked by another Dragonblood, they might well tell.<br /> But mostly the first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T05:12:11-07:00","id":901961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=899916#post899916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I have to write up a demon that steals faces.</div> </div> </div> </div>..... This got me thinking alittle... And I thought of Something Worse? (Potentially...)<br /> A Demon Who steals Identity and Fate from someone.... Probably a 2-3 Circle one... One Visit steals a Portion of your Fate (Making you suffer bad luck) Second Visit Steals some of your identity (You become forgetful and people don't reconigse you) third Visit your Features Dull and Fade abit, and a 4th Visit you Become one of its Thralls/Puppets. The Thralls are Probably 1st Circle Demons of a Type... To Make it Worse... No-one is Immune.. It just takes longer with Exalts.<br /> <br /> Edit: I Seem to be getting good at Derailing... Sorry for that. Just Ideas to good to Not Follow up on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 05-28-2016, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T05:16:47-07:00","id":901962,"title":"","content":"Also, Wizard, it's <i>Sesus</i> Nagezzar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T05:25:59-07:00","id":901964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901954#post901954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, nannies would obviously not criticise a Dragonblood, but if asked by another Dragonblood, they might well tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that people who work in the household of one of the Exalted are expected to keep all kinds of secrets (assuming they're not actually sorcerously bound against speaking them). Telling something like that... well, I think being thrown alive to the siaka(s?) is one of the best things you can hope for.<br /> <br /> That's assuming it's very likely for Dynasts to speak to one another's servants; I mean, if you're employing or coercing them for information that's one thing, but otherwise...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But mostly the first.</div> </div> </div> </div> You know, I've not watched all of Precious: based on the novel &quot;Push&quot; by Sapphire (about the first hour, I think), but I get the impression that Precious' father (who is also the father of both of her children, assuming she keeps the second one to term) doesn't live with her and her mother, and is somebody whom she rarely sees.<br /> <br /> Which is my roundabout way of saying &quot;if a Dynast is the type to sexually abuse their children, they're probably around enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Urrrgghh, now I've thought of a catty way of elaborating that, and am disgusted with myself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:00:42-07:00","id":901975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901964#post901964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine that people who work in the household of one of the Exalted are expected to keep all kinds of secrets (assuming they're not actually sorcerously bound against speaking them). Telling something like that... well, I think being thrown alive to the siaka(s?) is one of the best things you can hope for.<br /> <br /> That's assuming it's very likely for Dynasts to speak to one another's servants; I mean, if you're employing or coercing them for information that's one thing, but otherwise...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what the Realm considers of child abuse of this nature. If it is a serious matter in the law and the cultural views of the Realm, then a nanny could report on their master or mistress to a magistrate or other authority figure and let them deal with it, but it's likely to be a messy case by any standard. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901961#post901961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">..... This got me thinking alittle... And I thought of Something Worse? (Potentially...)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Demon Who steals Identity and Fate from someone.... Probably a 2-3 Circle one... One Visit steals a Portion of your Fate (Making you suffer bad luck) Second Visit Steals some of your identity (You become forgetful and people don't reconigse you) third Visit your Features Dull and Fade abit, and a 4th Visit you Become one of its Thralls/Puppets. The Thralls are Probably 1st Circle Demons of a Type... To Make it Worse... No-one is Immune.. It just takes longer with Exalts.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Can't we just rip of <a href=\"http://avatar.wikia.com/wiki/Koh\" target=\"_blank\">Koh</a> from the Last Airbender?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:06:08-07:00","id":901980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901962#post901962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Wizard, it's <i>Sesus</i> Nagezzar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... huh... I thought I'd written Sesus Negezzer. But I appear to have written Cynis. Dunno why. Thanks for pointing that out. And Sesus is one of my favourite houses, too (unlike Cynis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:11:44-07:00","id":901983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901975#post901975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what the Realm considers of child abuse of this nature. If it is a serious matter in the law and the cultural views of the Realm, then a nanny could report on their master or mistress to a magistrate or other authority figure and let them deal with it, but it's likely to be a messy case by any standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm... If it is a serious matter in the eyes of the Realm, doing anything about it might very well clash against the &quot;Dragon Blooded are morally elevated and grasp nuances you mortals wouldn't understand&quot;-mentality. So the priority might very well be to hush it up instead of wanting it reported and prosecuted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:16:31-07:00","id":901985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901983#post901983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... If it is a serious matter in the eyes of the Realm, doing anything about it might very well clash against the &quot;Dragon Blooded are morally elevated and grasp nuances you mortals wouldn't understand&quot;-mentality. So the priority might very well be to hush it up instead of wanting it reported and prosecuted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most people who work with children don't want to see them hurt. They may not report though official channels for fear of backlash, but they will find some way to help the child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:23:58-07:00","id":901986,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Exalted: the Dragon Blooded had something to say on the subject of child abuse...<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I think even that was about the subject of things like beatings. Probably would not even have the same restrictions on things like constantly deriding them.<br /> <br /> Besides, in many cases, I'd say there's a measure of ensuring plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good, you've done well, nanny. You're dismissed for the evening; kindly return to your quarters.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:33:48-07:00","id":901993,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2839\" data-vbnamecard=\"2839\">Lundgren</a>, these are the nannies and personal servants of a Dragon Blood, they might not have all the same misconceptions of Dragon Bloods due to their regular and prolonged proximity. Any arguement of the enlighted minds of the Terrestrial Exalt wouldn't fly with such people in these circumstances. There's only so much bullshit that can be justified with such an idea of &quot;Dragon Blooded are morally elevated and grasp nuances you mortals wouldn't understand&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a>, Now I can't help but write up an idea of a Solar whose's Exaltation came from trying to protect their Dragon Blood ward from an abusive parent. What caste to go with though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:38:26-07:00","id":901999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901985#post901985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people who work with children don't want to see them hurt. They may not report though official channels for fear of backlash, but they will find some way to help the child.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> But we also talk about a very large power disparity between the employer and employee. If a mortal would inform another Dynast, that mortal might end up in a world of trouble to keep the lid on, and they know it.<br /> <br /> Still, that doesn't have to mean the Dynast would ignore the situation, just that any attempt to deal with it might be behind the scenes. Which probably includes not wanting other Great Houses to find out about it.<br /> <br /> The most creepy version might be that the person decides to help the child rationalize it, and actually becoming an accomplice by normalizing the situation. &quot;I can at least try to be there for them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:38:52-07:00","id":902000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901993#post901993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a>, Now I can't help but write up an idea of a Solar whose's Exaltation came from trying to protect their Dragon Blood ward from an abusive parent. What caste to go with though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dawn! I want to see a Nanny wield a big ass sword and kick ass! <br /> <br /> Of course among this Nanny Anathema's list of crimes is &quot;kidnapping&quot;, though the Dragonblooded Ward will vehemently deny such charge. They are with their Nanny of their own volition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:42:05-07:00","id":902005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901993#post901993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2839\" data-vbnamecard=\"2839\">Lundgren</a>, these are the nannies and personal servants of a Dragon Blood, they might not have all the same misconceptions of Dragon Bloods due to their regular and prolonged proximity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say it depends on how they're conditioned. George Orwell wasn't basing doublethink on nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any arguement of the enlighted minds of the Terrestrial Exalt wouldn't fly with such people in these circumstances. There's only so much bullshit that can be justified with such an idea of &quot;Dragon Blooded are morally elevated and grasp nuances you mortals wouldn't understand&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> It would probably be nice to live in a society where openly acting like that wasn't the case in their presence was not the kind of thing that gets you murdered.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:49:03-07:00","id":902010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901993#post901993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a>, Now I can't help but write up an idea of a Solar whose's Exaltation came from trying to protect their Dragon Blood ward from an abusive parent. What caste to go with though?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on this... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Zenith is most likely an option. It would take lot of conviction for a mortal to stand up against a Dynast.<br /> Dawn if ready to physically stand in the way of a Dynast.<br /> Maybe an Eclipse if trying to talk to different people, and with subtle diplomacy trying to help.<br /> If trying to sneak the child out of there, or triggering an alarm or otherwise make sure some Dynast would catch the perpetrator, then I would guess a Night Caste.<br /> <br /> The only caste I can't think of a direct reason would be a Twilight. Still, it might very well be a possibility there as well. Maybe if building something that will tip of someone else that there is something going on?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T08:19:12-07:00","id":902058,"title":"","content":"Isator is right: what matters is not just what the nanny thinks, but how they'll be punished for suggesting that any Dynast is less than morally perfect and infallible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=901986#post901986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, Exalted: the Dragon Blooded had something to say on the subject of child abuse...</div> </div> </div> </div>What does it say? Please paraphrase/summarize?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T08:26:53-07:00","id":902061,"title":"","content":"Re: Realm Child Abuse, Exalted, General DB thoughts<br /> <br /> I just assumed that almost all Realm Patrician childhoods were essentially the extremes of 1980's American high school movies with more kicking ass, more privilege, and more mental illnesses brought on by a system designed to shape and mold you into a tool of the state while telling you that you are individually important (spiritually). I believe it's more or less IMPOSSIBLE without a lot of bending over backwards and ignoring things to portray a realm DB that doesn't have some kind of mental illness, psychosis, or lingering PTSD from the very environment in which they come from. I don't mean like fishmalk crazy, I mean things more akin to real world mental illnesses like BPD, etc.<br /> <br /> PC are exceptions and all, but I think it's something to keep in mind. The beneficiaries of such a system, the dragon blooded themselves, are being used and abused too under the aegis of tradition and other things.<br /> <br /> This might not square exactly with what I said above, but Dragon Bloods are my favorite splat, and the above is one of the reasons- because their plight is still on a certain level very much human, and very familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T10:53:05-07:00","id":902137,"title":"","content":"I always thought the primary school system is based on the realistic flaws of British boarding schools but portrayed through the lens of high-school anime tropes. Similar conclusions, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","user":"Shinjo","date":". 05-28-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:14:04-07:00","id":902156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902137#post902137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the primary school system is based on the realistic flaws of British boarding schools but portrayed through the lens of high-school anime tropes. Similar conclusions, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence also the Heptagram being described as R-rated Harry Potter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T13:42:09-07:00","id":902265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902156#post902156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence also the Heptagram being described as R-rated Harry Potter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't be ridiculous, R-rated Happy Potter would not be as awesome as the Heptagram - unless it has incest in it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:34:43-07:00","id":902328,"title":"","content":"Arent' the Scarlet Empress's sexual partners predominantly her own children/descendants?<br /> <br /> While I'm asking, where do the cofounders of new Houses come from if not the Houses? Are they all Lost Eggs? Who is V'neef's dad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/244-seagull","name":"Seagull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar244_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:08:57-07:00","id":902341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902328#post902328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arent' the Scarlet Empress's sexual partners predominantly her own children/descendants?<br /> <br /> While I'm asking, where do the cofounders of new Houses come from if not the Houses? Are they all Lost Eggs? Who is V'neef's dad?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all the Dragonblooded are descended from the Scarlet Empress. I think Peleps and one other house isn't of her bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:40:53-07:00","id":902363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902328#post902328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arent' the Scarlet Empress's sexual partners predominantly her own children/descendants?<br /> <br /> While I'm asking, where do the cofounders of new Houses come from if not the Houses? Are they all Lost Eggs? Who is V'neef's dad?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit depending on how few Dragon-bloods that were still standing at the end of the Great Contagion, but I would guess at least a couple of thousand. So they don't have to be closely related. But a few generations down the line, it might actually be hard to find someone not being able to trace their lineage to her while not being a Lost Egg.<br /> <br /> When it comes to founding a Great House, I would guess the first ones was primary her own children. But when it comes to a new Great House, it probably is a prominent family within another Great House. If you have seen the Godfather movies, there is at least one scene where one guy wants permission to start his own family. I imagine it being the same thing, just that a family in the Godfather is a Great House in Exalted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:05:10-07:00","id":902402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902328#post902328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arent' the Scarlet Empress's sexual partners predominantly her own children/descendants?</div> </div> </div> </div> {Hmm, this is probably focused on the consorts, official or unofficial, who are Exalted, rather than any random bed mate)<br /> <br /> I don't know about predominantly but... some are probably related to her. That distant, meaningless form of relation, where you need to have a genealogy table just to figure out who the common ancestor is, and the genetics are exactly as distinct as they would be from somebody with no observable common ancestor whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Although really, the distinction from mortals probably doesn't mean much anyway... the woman is about eight hundred years old, chances are that she has hundreds of thousands of mortal descendants at various strata of society. Dragon Blooded probably inevitably have mortal children (the &quot;probably&quot; comes from a question of whether they have more than one, and were lucky with the first and only), and that sends the line of their lineage off into mortal standards of generation and spreading out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm asking, where do the cofounders of new Houses come from if not the Houses?</div> </div> </div> </div> About half of those Houses were founded by about the halfway mark of the Realm.<br /> <br /> That's time enough for some people from the Shogunate to still be around. Indeed, a lot of institutions from the Realm would need to have been staffed in a different manner prior to that point.<br /> <br /> That's also about the time that the term &quot;Scarlet Dynasty&quot; came into use; prior to that, the ruling class of the Realm did not really have the overt characteristic of &quot;enormous extended family of the monarch&quot;. Likely, that was about the point when the notion that the Empress could conceivably live forever, and the question of succession had been horrifically complicated by the glut of available candidates.<br /> <br /> I would say the Empress is disinclined to have children with lovers from the Houses, for political reasons more than genetic ones. I would also think she's not inclined to do so with Outcastes for similar, combined with not wanting to introduce any wild card elements from their lineage into her pool of candidates to establish new Houses from should the need arise. I would say that what children she has have the fathers come from minor Houses, with such consorts having a lot less fanfare than the prominent figures of Tepet and Nellens and the like.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:56:18-07:00","id":902428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902341#post902341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all the Dragonblooded are descended from the Scarlet Empress. I think Peleps and one other house isn't of her bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tepet's the only one that we know had a history before the Scarlet Empire but we know so little about the origins of Peleps that it might be the case for them too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:01:02-07:00","id":902430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902428#post902428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tepet's the only one that we know had a history before the Scarlet Empire but we know so little about the origins of Peleps that it might be the case for them too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be confusing tepet with peleps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:03:08-07:00","id":902432,"title":"","content":"Do you mean House Tepet, or consort Tepet?<br /> <br /> There have been a few offhand references to Peleps founded by a daughter of the Empress, but I can only assume that a lot of freelancers have forgotten about it while writing about Houses or the history of the Realm. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:04:06-07:00","id":902434,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that, based on how the Dynast Houses have been depicted up to this point, the common ancestor the Empress and her prospective lover would share would be the Empress herself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/244-seagull","name":"Seagull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar244_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:27:19-07:00","id":902443,"title":"","content":"Those Houses are certainly descended from her at this point even if the consorts weren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-28-2016, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T20:06:29-07:00","id":902458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=902434#post902434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine that, based on how the Dynast Houses have been depicted up to this point, the common ancestor the Empress and her prospective lover would share would be the Empress herself.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWhen discussing common ancestors in genealogy, it needs to be somebody who is an actual ancestor; you cannot be an ancestor to yourself.<br /> <br /> The closest common ancestor between yourself and most people whom you are related to, including one of your parents, is a grandparent. As you spread a search more laterally, the common ancestor goes further back; the siblings of your grandparents, and anybody descended from them, have a common ancestor in your great-grandparent, and so on.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T20:07:36-07:00","id":903921,"title":"","content":"I figure these kind of abuses happen about as much as they happen in the real world, considering human nature is what it is. I also think the Great Houses hush it up almost as an afterthought, then take it into account along with how valuable the perpetrator is to the House when determining their stipend and what resources they have access to. As callous as it sounds, there's probably a cost/benefit line that has to be crossed before someone in power steps in and actually stops it, otherwise it's up to the victim to mitigate it as best they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T20:36:38-07:00","id":903926,"title":"","content":"Honestly it probably happens a bit more than it does in real life, at least among the Dragon Blooded. It's one of the problems with them essentially having absolute power and being above the law. The only authority most Dragon Blooded answer to is their House leader, who may or may not particularly care about what's going on in someone else's House. And of course, if it is the House leader, you're hosed. The only person with anything approaching authority over the House leaders is gone (and let's be honest, the Empress probably wouldn't have cared much anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T21:24:02-07:00","id":903942,"title":"","content":"I think the house leader will normally care when the victim is a dynastic kid, because that's a potential future Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T21:31:38-07:00","id":903945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=903926#post903926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it probably happens a bit more than it does in real life, at least among the Dragon Blooded. It's one of the problems with them essentially having absolute power and being above the law. The only authority most Dragon Blooded answer to is their House leader, who may or may not particularly care about what's going on in someone else's House. And of course, if it is the House leader, you're hosed. The only person with anything approaching authority over the House leaders is gone (and let's be honest, the Empress probably wouldn't have cared much anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but by the same token, you're probably going to have more outraged, idealistic(ish) heroes righteously kicking the crap out of the offenders, politics and prudence be damned - literal hot-blooded shonen power cuts both ways here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T21:38:48-07:00","id":903949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=903942#post903942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the house leader will normally care when the victim is a dynastic kid, because that's a potential future Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may or may not. It would definitely depend on the House leader (I imagine, for example, that Nellens' council would be much more proactive in taking Dragon Blooded to task for abusing their lessers,as many members of the Council are normal humans). Even still, realistically about the only thing they could do would be to cut the individual's stipend. It's not like there are police you can call or jails you can put Dragon Blooded in. That's also definitely not the kind of story you want other people discussing about your House at the local salon, so the House would just cover it up and keep it quiet. <br /> <br /> In general, in organizations that try to solve things internally and keep those kinds of abuses quiet quiet, it often ends with the perpetrators getting a slap on the wrist, if that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:50:15-07:00","id":903971,"title":"","content":"Oh, I definitely see it as something they'll want to deal with in-house.<br /> My expectation is that, generally speaking, DBs who do bad stuff in their house get sent to jobs in the Threshold. Like Sesus Chenow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:03:12-07:00","id":903975,"title":"","content":"The question is, is it consensual? If not, DUEL TO THE DEATH!!!! If it is, live in happy secrecy. If brought up in polite conversation, DUEL TO THE DEATH!!!!! Dragonblooded society( or exalted in general) are a warrior/knight/samurai society by nature. Everyone is polite, unless they are looking for a fight. Argument between Husbands and wives might end up with both of them is full armor and daiklaive outside their home( why outside? Its vulgar to fight in someones house, how droll!!). Rules and conventions in DB society is to limit loss of DB life and damage to property. But they are all living weapons. IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:47:25-07:00","id":903991,"title":"","content":"Fighting, possibly, but not to the death. DBs aren't supposed to kill other DBs.<br /> That's what poison and proxis are for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:33:19-07:00","id":904653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=903945#post903945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but by the same token, you're probably going to have more outraged, idealistic(ish) heroes righteously kicking the crap out of the offenders, politics and prudence be damned - literal hot-blooded shonen power cuts both ways here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that unlikely. Power disparities don't equalize the rates of abuse, they increase it. I would argue the #1 cause of solar personality defects in the First Age wasn't the Great Curse, but society continuously telling them that they were above morality and that almost everything they do, up to and including killing innocents, was morally pristine. Similarly, I would argue that the #1 cause of terrestrial personality defects in the Second Age isn't the Great Curse, but again, a religion that teaches them they're God's gift to mankind.<br /> <br /> There isn't really much precedent in Earth history for this sort of thing -- the way 1A solars or 2A DBs are treated, historically speaking, almost never applies to entire social classes, but are more similar to the reverence cults have for their leaders. They aren't outright worshiped as gods, but they are viewed as inherently superior and more enlightened (which may be true). Abuse tends to flourish in that sort of situation.<br /> <br /> There's also the question of what moral norms even exist in Creation? We know of exceptions (the West, etc.) but we don't know what is normal for Creation dwellers or where those norms came from. The only real possibility I can think of is that they came from the First Age, which did have some sort of notion that people deserved certain rights (like access to I AM), but I don't know what rights they had back then. And the DBs didn't have a rosy view of that era.<br /> <br /> So I can't even begin to guess what rights non-exalted people are viewed as having in Creation, if they even have a concept of rights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:42:08-07:00","id":904689,"title":"","content":"I don't think people in the Realm believe in universal human rights... but I do think they believe in the rights of Dynasts. Including Dynastic children.<br /> <br /> This is why I think abusive dynasts are far more likely to abuse slaves or peasants than their own children (who they don't see that often anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:52:20-07:00","id":904736,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree they'd be protective of their own children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T00:36:48-07:00","id":904771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=903975#post903975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, is it consensual? If not, DUEL TO THE DEATH!!!! <br /> \u2026<br /> Rules and conventions in DB society is to limit loss of DB life and damage to property. But they are all living weapons. IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick any two gods, big alien monsters, superheroes, et cetera., from the last ten years' worth of big-budget blockbusters. Recall the kinds of destruction they typically wreak when the level of discourse rises above &quot;stern disagreement.&quot; Now ask yourself, <i>why</i> would one foster a culture in which these behemoths are trained from birth that the <i>immediate</i> default way of settling qualms is high-action fights to the death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-01-2016, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:30:30-07:00","id":904787,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the Dynasts view of protecting their own children from abuse; it might be worth to remember that what is considered abuse can vary a lot between different cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:07:05-07:00","id":904897,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I wonder if getting abused counts as one of the stress-types that can help along an exaltation in young DBs. If so... I think being ruled by a bunch of super powered trauma victims might be a good case for the Gold faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:12:15-07:00","id":904904,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go with &quot;Abuse is as the same level in real life with a chance of the victim Exalting and kicking the abuser's ass&quot;. <br /> <br /> Now, Dynast children are still under a lot of stress -similar to Harvard bound children- but nothing too over the top. I imagine in the late teens there is some sort of boot camp to try to encourage Exaltation as a last ditch effort. Of course the kids probably want to be there, because they are desperate to Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:39:24-07:00","id":905105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=904771#post904771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pick any two gods, big alien monsters, superheroes, et cetera., from the last ten years' worth of big-budget blockbusters. Recall the kinds of destruction they typically wreak when the level of discourse rises above &quot;stern disagreement.&quot; Now ask yourself, <i>why</i> would one foster a culture in which these behemoths are trained from birth that the <i>immediate</i> default way of settling qualms is high-action fights to the death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're writing a setting for an epic kung-fu action game and not bleak survival horror under a dystopian regime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:47:25-07:00","id":905151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905105#post905105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you're writing a setting for an epic kung-fu action game and not bleak survival horror under a dystopian regime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, Exalted could easily become the later if not for the Chosen being powerful enough to break mountains and destroy cities.<br /> Shame about the mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:58:34-07:00","id":905158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=904904#post904904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go with &quot;Abuse is as the same level in real life with a chance of the victim Exalting and kicking the abuser's ass&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the understanding that there are far fewer options for victims than there are in the modern world. There are no police officers or social workers who might notice that something's wrong and intervene. There aren't really any authority figures the child could confide in (home tutors and servants wouldn't have the power to do anything). Realistically, the only people the victim could tell that would have any positive outcome would be the abusers parents, and that might not even be possible if the family isn't particularly close. Plus, it requires a tremendous amount of trust to confide that sort of thing in someone, and I imagine there aren't too many dynastic children with that close of a relationship to their grandparents. <br /> <br /> Most victims probably do dream of Exalting as turning the tables on their tormentor, but it doesn't happen anywhere near as often as it poetically should. For too many victims, childhood would probably nothing more than a dark cave with no possibility of escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:02:56-07:00","id":905160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905158#post905158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the understanding that there are far fewer options for victims than there are in the modern world. There are no police officers or social workers who might notice that something's wrong and intervene. There aren't really any authority figures the child could confide in (home tutors and servants wouldn't have the power to do anything). Realistically, the only people the victim could tell that would have any positive outcome would be the abusers parents, and that might not even be possible if the family isn't particularly close. Plus, it requires a tremendous amount of trust to confide that sort of thing in someone, and I imagine there aren't too many dynastic children with that close of a relationship to their grandparents.<br /> <br /> Most victims probably do dream of Exalting as turning the tables on their tormentor, but it doesn't happen anywhere near as often as it poetically should. For too many victims, childhood would probably nothing more than a dark cave with no possibility of escape.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. Victims of Abuse have few options. However, I don't want the default state of a Dynast's Childhood to be &quot;Abuse&quot;. Unless you count high pressure to succeed/exalt as abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:06:54-07:00","id":905162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905160#post905160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree. Victims of Abuse have few options. However, I don't want the default state of a Dynast's Childhood to be &quot;Abuse&quot;. Unless you count high pressure to succeed/exalt as abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it definitely isn't. Most Dragon Blooded wouldn't be interested in attacking their own children (just as most people aren't). It's one of those things that probably does happen though, more often than people would prefer to think it does.<br /> <br /> I imagine though most Dragon Blooded abuse tends towards harsh, corporal punishments, mental abuse and the sorts of things we think of when it comes to &quot;tiger parenting.&quot; Sexual abuse is unlikely to be much more common than it is in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:09:21-07:00","id":905295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=904771#post904771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pick any two gods, big alien monsters, superheroes, et cetera., from the last ten years' worth of big-budget blockbusters. Recall the kinds of destruction they typically wreak when the level of discourse rises above &quot;stern disagreement.&quot; Now ask yourself, <i>why</i> would one foster a culture in which these behemoths are trained from birth that the <i>immediate</i> default way of settling qualms is high-action fights to the death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Violence is not the default. Look at the second part you quoted. But its ALWAYS the backup option. I picture DB society to be very polite to each other, just like Regency Era London, England mixed with Shogunate Era Japan . At least to each others face. Even House Leaders don't act with impunity, cause their DB followers might summon there demon army, fanatical super elite Legionary Dragon unit, or break out legendary weapon of primordial/solar slaying/ city killer to answer the insult. But talking, playing chess/card, lesser political appointmens/exile or partying harder than your opponent/rival is probably the better way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T20:53:19-07:00","id":905379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905160#post905160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I don't want the default state of a Dynast's Childhood to be &quot;Abuse&quot;. Unless you count high pressure to succeed/exalt as abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree. The usual motives for child sexual abuse (lack of availability or twisted parental bond) are largely absent for Dynasts, as DBs are never short on partners, slaves, or victims, and they barely interact with their own children.<br /> <br /> Its a real shame about *every common born mortal in the setting* though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:28:38-07:00","id":905428,"title":"","content":"&quot;I was never a pretty or particularly fit child. In addition to my formidable grasp of martial lore, I was always unusually focused, undistracted by many of the things that make a child a child. This often resulted in a fair amount of ridicule at the hands of other children and was a cause of expressed worry from my mother and the other Dragon-Blooded who visited our home. Nonetheless, there were benefits. The first advantage that I noticed was the freedom this granted me. When my mother held feasts at our home,I was never chosen to be the performing monkey. Instead, I was left alone, uninterrupted, with my books and hobbies, the distracted child who existed out of sight and mind. This was far from the greatest benefit, however. For when, after these galas, my fair-faced brothers and sisters were led to the bedchambers of some visiting Cynis lord or the bath of our dear Uncle Sesus, I was left, dreaming in my very own bed, without a care in the world. Unfortunately, when the next morning came, and we gathered around the table to break our fast, the looks and jabs of resentment from my brothers and sisters were undeniable and lasting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Aspect Book Wood.<br /> <br /> I imagine that this may be relevant to the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:57:46-07:00","id":905436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905428#post905428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I was never a pretty or particularly fit child. In addition to my formidable grasp of martial lore, I was always unusually focused, undistracted by many of the things that make a child a child. This often resulted in a fair amount of ridicule at the hands of other children and was a cause of expressed worry from my mother and the other Dragon-Blooded who visited our home. Nonetheless, there were benefits. The first advantage that I noticed was the freedom this granted me. When my mother held feasts at our home,I was never chosen to be the performing monkey. Instead, I was left alone, uninterrupted, with my books and hobbies, the distracted child who existed out of sight and mind. This was far from the greatest benefit, however. For when, after these galas, my fair-faced brothers and sisters were led to the bedchambers of some visiting Cynis lord or the bath of our dear Uncle Sesus, I was left, dreaming in my very own bed, without a care in the world. Unfortunately, when the next morning came, and we gathered around the table to break our fast, the looks and jabs of resentment from my brothers and sisters were undeniable and lasting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Aspect Book Wood.<br /> <br /> I imagine that this may be relevant to the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just popping in to saw ew that made me squirm in my chair uncomfortably. Kudos to the writers for conveying that godawful feeling.<br /> Seriously. It really shows clearly what at least his family was like, and that he was greatful to avoid the horrid shit his siblings had to endure. <br /> <br /> However yes it shows some inscest did possibly occur it did say &quot;some visiting cynis lord OR uncle sesus.&quot; was uncle Sesus uncle by blood or marriage?...because as much as it sickens me to say there is a difference, and rather or not its considered inscest if you are not blood related is iffy.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying its OKAY if you are not blood related so please dont think that! I'm just saying from the info we have, we can only make assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:08:57-07:00","id":905438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905436#post905436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However yes it shows some inscest did possibly occur it did say &quot;some visiting cynis lord OR uncle sesus.&quot; was uncle Sesus uncle by blood or marriage?...because as much as it sickens me to say there is a difference, and rather or not its considered inscest if you are not blood related is iffy.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying its OKAY if you are not blood related so please dont think that! I'm just saying from the info we have, we can only make assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the guy telling the story was Sesus Nagezzer (the Slug) so.....<br /> <br /> Also, because of the way he just says Sesus, I would imagine that he is talking about the Empresses son.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","user":"Ghost","date":". 06-02-2016, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:14:56-07:00","id":905439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905438#post905438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the guy telling the story was Sesus Nagezzer (the Slug) so.....<br /> <br /> Also, because of the way he just says Sesus, I would imagine that he is talking about the Empresses son.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OH okay thats where I got lost, I wasnt sure 100% who was telling the story, I didnt read that book, and i'll be damned if i'm googling shit at this hour of night I'll never get off the internet if i start down that black hole.<br /> <br /> So then it would be inscest in this case then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:26:54-07:00","id":905443,"title":"","content":"Sesus is the grand patriarch of his family. However, there is a little bit of a discrepancy between 1E and 2E on this. In 2E his write up says that the Empress is his grandmother which would make Sesus his father, but in 1E he calls him uncle and his mom is Sesus' sister while his father is a mortal. That would mean that her mom is the Empresses daughter that, for some reason, does not have her own great house. I'm not sure what to make of that lore wise, but I noticed that since I like the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","user":"Ghost","date":". 06-02-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:35:54-07:00","id":905447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905443#post905443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sesus is the grand patriarch of his family. However, there is a little bit of a discrepancy between 1E and 2E on this. In 2E his write up says that the Empress is his grandmother which would make Sesus his father, but in 1E he calls him uncle and his mom is Sesus' sister while his father is a mortal. That would mean that her mom is the Empresses daughter that, for some reason, does not have her own great house. I'm not sure what to make of that lore wise, but I noticed that since I like the character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That made my head hurt. I understand though, its likely a smallish lore error. But at fear of derailing, i cant recal does every daughter/son of the empress have a great house under their name? It could be possible she never founded one maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:17:42-07:00","id":905467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905447#post905447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That made my head hurt. I understand though, its likely a smallish lore error. But at fear of derailing, i cant recal does every daughter/son of the empress have a great house under their name? It could be possible she never founded one maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, it's just kinda weird. I don't remember if it was ever spelled out but it was implied that her Redness' kids all had a great house. Perhaps they were twins and shared the house? More likely is that the writers just didn't think that part though in 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:26:18-07:00","id":905493,"title":"","content":"Exalted: the Dragon Blooded outright says that the majority of the children of the Scarlet Empress have achieved little of note.<br /> <br /> \u200bGreat Houses are not an entitlement of every child of the Empress, they are something formed to fill political conveniences and/or a reward for children who display particular talents. Ragara was one of the earliest Houses formed around a child, and was something made to take over a lot of the assets left behind by a House that rebelled at the behest of a robot, with Ragara himself having been a key actor in quelling that uprising.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:49:20-07:00","id":905505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905443#post905443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sesus is the grand patriarch of his family. However, there is a little bit of a discrepancy between 1E and 2E on this. In 2E his write up says that the Empress is his grandmother which would make Sesus his father, but in 1E he calls him uncle and his mom is Sesus' sister while his father is a mortal. That would mean that her mom is the Empresses daughter that, for some reason, does not have her own great house. I'm not sure what to make of that lore wise, but I noticed that since I like the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of the Empress who are in another great house are mentioned a few times in both 1st and 2nd ed. And, as was just said by Isator, many children of the Empress are not particularly famous.<br /> <br /> Consider that there's been 23 Great Houses, a lot of which (Nellens, Tepet, the Houses that predated Ragara) were Houses for her husband (and his kids), not a specific kid.<br /> I am sure she has had more than 23 kids in her over 800 years of life.<br /> <br /> So, I assume when one is famous enough to found their own great house, their brothers and sisters* normally join them, to give the new house more than just one guy and his kids. And because, by now, the Great Houses are how the system works, so if you're an un-Housed DB, even a kid of the Empress, interacting with the Realm government is awkward. You have no voice in the Deliberative, for example. So it makes sense to stick them in a House. Or perhaps it's minor half-siblings and siblings with the same aspect, or something like that.<br /> <br /> Of course, we probably shouldn't make too much of Negezzer's write-up: for one thing, at one point his father was a V'neef (hence his Wood aspect), which considering V'neef is a pretty new house, seems somewhat unlikely.<br /> And there are plenty of other inconsistencies in both the 2nd ed and 1st ed depictions of Dynastic politics, geneologies, and timelines.<br /> <br /> *Bear in mind that most of the Empress's children are half-siblings. So Sesus's sister is in House Sesus, while Mnemon and Ragara are only his half-siblings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm... looking back at what I just said:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that there's been 23 Great Houses, a lot of which (Nellens, Tepet, the Houses that predated Ragara) were Houses for her husband (and his kids), not a specific kid.<br /> I am sure she has had more than 23 kids in her over 800 years of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if she had any children, or relatives of any kind, when she became Empress. Like, I could well see her giving her nephews and nieces a privileged position, in a way that eventually grew into a Great House.<br /> I also wonder whether some of the original Houses (like Manosque, Jerah, Chanos, etc) were even her close relatives at all. I could well imagine a Shogunate Gens still around, in reduced form, on the Isle, swearing loyalty to her, and developing into what were to become Great Houses.<br /> These might not necessarily still exist today (or they could have changed their name when their leader married her son, for example), but I'd wonder if the early Realm was a rather more messy and less centralised government than it is today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-02-2016, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:16:58-07:00","id":905515,"title":"","content":"I think that of the 23 Great Houses, most of the ones that we don't see anymore were established around things other than relations to the Empress, and that their elimination has been an ongoing goal of her consolidation of power.<br /> <br /> \u200bLook at something like House Jerah; that's been around as early as, what, Realm year forty? Decades before her first child, and when her first husband (who was not called Jerah) was still alive?<br /> <br /> It looks to me that the early history of the Realm had the Empress (perhaps with some Sidereal guidance) originate the concept of organising Dragon Blooded strictly along family lines as a way of marshalling them to increase their numbers and concentrating them into more manageable packages, so she took a lot of the surviving Exalted (who would likely have been of varying backgrounds and social status in the Shogunate), putting them together and saying &quot;right, you're a family now; you're going to be handed offices and materials as a whole, and here's how marriages are going to work&quot;.<br /> <br /> (My own pet theory is that a lot of these Shogunate elites were also investing into the early government of the Empress, putting forward their own resources to help kickstart civilisation in exchange for a stake in the new power structures and being repaid over time; I think of the stipends of Great Houses as existing within a technical legal basis of repayment of debts, even if the bonds on those debts have been transferred from defunct Houses to newer ones)<br /> <br /> It was only ever a temporary measure to help get things up and running at the beginning, get some new life into the Exalted devastated by the Contagion, and ensure a spirit of cooperation; uprisings and assassination attempts added urgency to the need to transfer those powers to something conceivably more pliant. Examples like Manosque and Jerah are notably dramatic, but most Great Houses have fallen more quietly, with the Empress seizing on opportunities to cut off their privileges and revenue streams and transfer their assets to new Houses, that were built around direct ceremonial ties to her, sweeping away the remnants of the old regime to establish something whose culture perceived her as more of a fixture.<br /> <br /> That process may be virtually complete, or may have had a few loose ends hanging, depending on how one assigns Houses that either have no apparent child or consort associated with them, or statements of such are sporadic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:24:59-07:00","id":905523,"title":"","content":"That would fit much better with how state-building has generally worked historically, with a slow centralisation of powers in the hands of the ruling dynasty and an erosion of the rights of other titles, than having only a monarchy that everyone marries into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:38:27-07:00","id":905818,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall even the idea of &quot;the Dynasty&quot; didn't come about for a few centuries. I think it was 200 or 300 years before the Empress gave her Lost Egg speach, stating her desire to bring all the Dragon Blooded into her bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:54:19-07:00","id":905827,"title":"","content":"By the time of the Empress' disappearance, the Great Houses are either descended from her or from one of her consorts. I imagine those Houses with no major bloodties to the Empress fall under the Minor House category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:55:41-07:00","id":905829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/899895-squicky-question-about-dragon-blooded?p=905827#post905827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the time of the Empress' disappearance, the Great Houses are either descended from her or from one of her consorts. I imagine those Houses with no major bloodties to the Empress fall under the Minor House category.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Empress could have &quot;Adopted&quot; some influential house founders too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T12:14:48-07:00","id":905849,"title":"","content":"Guess worth mentioning in the preview of DB 3e, there are going to be a lot of contenders for the throne this time around from Great houses, including a civil war between houses even minor ones...hell it is even assumed that the PC dragon-blooded are contenders for the throne as well. As they put it in the preview that the Scarlet Empress wasn't the oldest, wisest or even most powerful exalt among her peers back then...she just happened to have the balls to seize the opportunity and take on every challenges.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T13:25:19-07:00","id":905911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> 